# Visual Explainer Output

This repository publishes the contents of `docs/` to GitHub Pages on every push to `main`.

When using the `visual-explainer` skill — diagrams, architecture overviews, diff reviews, plan reviews, project recaps, slide decks, or complex comparison tables — follow the skill at `.cursor/skills/visual-explainer/SKILL.md`, then apply this output override:

1. Write the generated HTML to `docs/visual-explainer/<descriptive-name>.html`. Use a kebab-case basename. Do not write to `~/.agent/diagrams/`.
2. Do not overwrite an existing page unless the user asked to replace it.
3. After writing, report the repo-relative path and the published URL: `https://texarkanine.github.io/rmf/visual-explainer/<filename>.html`.
4. Leave `docs/index.html` alone. The Pages workflow rebuilds the listing from the HTML files in `docs/visual-explainer/`.

This rule covers visual-explainer HTML pages only. Mermaid embedded in Markdown still belongs in the document that needs it.
